# Backend API & Upload Proxies (Render API Web Service)
/api/*       https://hasaca-api.onrender.com/api/:splat     200!
/uploads/*   https://hasaca-api.onrender.com/uploads/:splat 200!

# sitemap.xml is per-tenant/host-derived (backend/server.js) — proxied so the real dynamic
# version is served instead of the static placeholder file at the repo root. Bots tolerate
# Render's free-tier cold start fine for this one; a slow/failed sitemap fetch just gets
# retried by Search Console later, no global consequence.
/sitemap.xml https://hasaca-api.onrender.com/sitemap.xml    200!

# robots.txt is served as a STATIC file (below, no Render proxy) on purpose — see phase-82.md.
# When this route WAS proxied to Render, a cold Render dyno made the robots.txt fetch itself
# time out, and Google (per the robots.txt spec: unreachable robots.txt = assume everything is
# disallowed) responded by blocking indexing of the ENTIRE site, not just one page — confirmed
# live via Search Console's URL Inspection ("Robots.txt tarafından engellendi"). robots.txt
# doesn't need per-tenant logic on this shared marketing domain (no tenant context resolves for
# a bare host request here anyway), so trading the Render-side seo_robots dynamism for a file
# Netlify can always serve instantly removed the failure mode outright. Tenant CUSTOM domains
# still get the real dynamic per-tenant robots.txt from backend/server.js, since those point
# straight at Render and never touch this file (see tenantSeo.js's own note on this).

